OL,3,GNEWSAFirst cow tests positive for
OL,4,Abluetongue virus in Scotland
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe first case of the potentially fatal
OL,7,Fbluetongue virus in a cow has been
OL,8,Fconfirmed in Scotland.
OL,10,FThe National Farmers Union Scotland
OL,11,F(NFUS) said the animal tested positive
OL,12,Fon a farm in Dumfries and Galloway. It
OL,13,Fis the fourth farm to be affected by
OL,14,Fthe virus in Scotland.
OL,16,FBluetongue was confirmed in a lamb and
OL,17,Fthree sheep on three farms within a 2km
OL,18,F(1.2 miles) area around Creetown last
OL,19,Fweek.
OL,23,APub: 17-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
